{{Quote|Giving new and existing fans the final chapter of ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' has been our honor at Disney+, and we are overjoyed by the global response to this landmark series. While ''The Clone Wars'' may have come to its conclusion, our partnership with the groundbreaking storytellers and artists at Lucasfilm Animation is only beginning. We are thrilled to bring Dave Filoni's vision to life through the next adventures of the ''Bad Batch''.|Agnes Chu announcing ''The Bad Batch''|<ref name="Announcement" />}}
'''''Star Wars: The Bad Batch''''' is an animated television series that acts as both a sequel to and a spin-off of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''. It focuses on the [[squad]] known as [[Clone Force 99]], a band of genetically enhanced clone troopers. It was announced on [[July 13]], [[2020]] and premiered on [[Disney+]] on [[May 4]], [[2021]].<ref name="Announcement" /> The [[The Bad Batch Season 1|first season]] has sixteen episodes,<ref name="Season length">{{WebCite|url=https://www.cnet.com/news/star-wars-the-bad-batch-crew-talks-season-length-omega-and-imperial-oppression|text=Star Wars: The Bad Batch crew talks season length, Omega and Imperial oppression|author=Keane, Sean|date=2021-05-03|work=[[Wikipedia:CNET|CNET]]|archivedate=20210503173054}}</ref> and its musical score was composed by [[Kevin Kiner]], who previously worked on ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' and ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''.<ref name="Full of Sith">{{WebCite|url=http://fullofsith.com/archives/3552|text=Episode CDIX: Kevin Kiner and the Bad Batch|archivedate=20210421191158}}</ref>

The series stars [[Dee Bradley Baker]] as all [[Gender|male]] members of [[Clone Force 99|The Bad Batch]], including [[Hunter]], [[Wrecker]], [[Tech]], [[Echo]], and [[Crosshair]],<ref name="SYFY" /> as well as [[Michelle Ang]] as [[Omega]].<ref name="CNET" />

==Official description==
''The series follows the elite and experimental clones of the Bad Batch (first introduced in ''The Clone Wars'') as they find their way into a rapidly changing galaxy in the immediate aftermath of the Clone War. Members of Bad Batch (Clone Force 99) — a unique squad of clones who vary genetically from their brothers in the Clone Army — each possess a singular exceptional skill, which makes them extraordinarily effective soldiers and a formidable crew. In the post-Clone Wars era, they will take on daring mercenary missions as they struggle to stay afloat and find new purpose.''<ref name="Announcement" />

==Development==
{{Quote|During our first year on Disney+, our animated series ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'', saw tremendous success with its epic seventh and final season. Building on the legacy of ''The Clone Wars'', our new animated series ''The Bad Batch'', follows the specialist commandos of Clone Force 99 as they embark on new missions in a rapidly changing galaxy.|Kathleen Kennedy, on ''The Bad Batch'' during the Disney Investor Day 2020|<ref name="Investor2020">{{DisneyCompany|url=disney-investor-day-2020|text=Disney Investor Day 2020}}</ref>}}
''The Bad Batch'' was announced on [[July 13]], [[2020]], along with the producers and writers attached to the show. [[Dave Filoni]], [[Athena Yvette Portillo]], [[Brad Rau]], and [[Jennifer Corbett]] were named as executive producers. [[Carrie Beck]] also served as co-executive producer and [[Josh Rimes]] as producer. Rau also served as supervising director while Corbett was named as the series' head writer.<ref name="Announcement" /> Corbett intended to ground ''The Bad Batch''{{'s}} stories to the real world, and the series creators particularly focused on military veterans who "no longer have a war to fight" and find themselves unemployed and in need of support.<ref name="TBB end interview" /> A number of [[LEGO Star Wars|LEGO ''Star Wars'']] sets based on ''The Bad Batch'' released.<ref name="LEGO  Bad Batch">{{SW|url=news/lego-star-wars-the-bad-batch-attack-shuttle-exclusive-reveal|text=The LEGO Group's ''Star Wars: The Bad Batch'' Attack Shuttle Comes in for a Landing - Exclusive Reveal}}</ref>

[[File:BadBatchLego.png|thumb|right|250px|''LEGO Star Wars: The Bad Batch'']]
On [[August 5]], [[2021]], the series was renewed for a [[The Bad Batch Season 2|second season]].<ref name="Season Two Announcement">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-bad-batch-season-2|text=Disney+ Announces Season 2 of ''Star Wars: The Bad Batch''}}</ref>

On [[April 10]], [[2023]], the series was renewed for a [[The Bad Batch Season 3|third and final season]].<ref name="S3 Announcement" />

==Release and reception==
The first trailer for the first season of the ''Bad Batch'' was unveiled at a [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] investors presentation on [[December 10]], 2020.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|YB9DIxdB198|Sizzle &#124; The Bad Batch &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/sizzle-the-bad-batch}}</ref> A second trailer was released on [[March 30]], [[2021]].<ref name="Bad Batch Trailer">{{SWYouTube|BsOmYpP4UDU|Star Wars: The Bad Batch &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/trailer-the-bad-batch}}</ref>

On [[May 29]] [[2022]], Lucasfilm released the official trailer for the series' second season at the [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|''Star Wars'' Celebration Anaheim 2022]].<ref name="SWCA 2022">{{SW|url=news/swca-2022-the-bad-batch-season-2-panel|text=SWCA 2022: 6 Highlights from the ''Star Wars: The Bad Batch'' Season 2 Panel}}</ref><ref name="Season Two Official Trailer">{{SWYouTube|6JX5OW8cOec|Star Wars: The Bad Batch &#124; Season 2 Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+}}</ref>

On [[January 22]] [[2024]], Lucasfilm released the official trailer for the series' third season.<ref name="Season Three Official Trailer">{{SWYouTube|Oa5zeHdSwdQ|The Bad Batch &#124; The Final Season Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/the-bad-batch-the-final-season-official-trailer-disney}}</ref>

The first episode of ''The Bad Batch'' premiered on [[Disney+]] on [[May 4]], 2021 with a 74-minute<ref name="Aftermath" /> [[Aftermath (episode)|premiere episode]].<ref name="D23 May">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-may-2021|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in May 2021|nolive=1}}</ref> The [[The Bad Batch Season 1|first season]] ran for 16 episodes until [[August 13]], 2021.<ref name="Season length">{{WebCite|url=https://www.cnet.com/news/star-wars-the-bad-batch-crew-talks-season-length-omega-and-imperial-oppression|text=Star Wars: The Bad Batch crew talks season length, Omega and Imperial oppression|author=Keane, Sean|date=2021-05-03|work=[[Wikipedia:CNET|CNET]]|archivedate=20210503173054}}</ref><ref name="D23 August">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-august-2021|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in August 2021}}</ref>

The [[The Bad Batch Season 2|second season]] ran for 16 episodes from [[January 4]] to [[March 29]], [[2023]].<ref name="D23">{{SW|url=news/d23-expo-2022-lucasfilm|text=D23 Expo 2022: All the Big Lucasfilm Reveals for ''Andor'', ''Willow'', ''The Mandalorian'', and More}}</ref><ref name="Season 2 Dates">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-bad-batch-season-2-trailer-key-art|text=Clone Force 99 Is Back in New ''Star Wars: The Bad Batch'' Season 2 Trailer}}</ref>

The [[The Bad Batch Season 3|third season]] premiered on [[February 21]], [[2024]].<ref name="OfficialTrailer">{{SWYouTube|Oa5zeHdSwdQ|The Bad Batch &#124; The Final Season Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/the-bad-batch-the-final-season-official-trailer-disney}}</ref>

